WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.680
This week, we're going to be talking about chunks, compact packages of information that

2
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.319
your mind can easily access.

3
00:00:11.319 --> 00:00:15.760
We'll talk about how you can form chunks, how you can use them to improve your understanding

4
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:22.360
of and creativity with the material, and how chunks can help you do better on tests.

5
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.500
We'll also talk about illusions of competence in learning.

6
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.420
This is when you're using ineffective study methods that fool your mind into thinking

7
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.979
you're learning something, when you're mostly just wasting your time.

8
00:00:33.979 --> 00:00:39.680
We'll cover what those less effective study methods are, and tell you what methods research

9
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.979
has shown will work better to help you in your studies.

10
00:00:42.979 --> 00:00:49.700
Finally, we'll talk about something called overlearning, which can solidly ingrain information

11
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.419
in your mind, but also can be a little like digging deeper ruts as you might spin your

12
00:00:54.419 --> 00:00:56.779
wheels ineffectively in learning.

13
00:00:56.779 --> 00:01:03.180
You can make your study time more valuable by interleaving, providing intelligent variety

14
00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.540
in your studies.

15
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.139
I'm Barbara Oakley.

16
00:01:06.139 --> 00:01:07.900
Thanks for learning how to learn.